ScheduTeach (SchEDU Teach) — Production Readiness Review
Methodology note (read first): This is a full-source + full-schema audit — every route, component, lib, edge function, and all 16 SQL files were traced UI → API → DB. I did not run the app on a physical device (no runtime/emulator was available), so visual-pixel and live-network findings are inferred from code; every such inference is cited to file:line so you can confirm. Findings from runtime-only checks (exact contrast ratios, real device reflow) are flagged as "verify on device."

The single most important framing fact: ScheduTeach is not an LMS. It is a teacher lesson-planning + scheduling tool for the Philippine DepEd context. The review template you supplied assumes a full classroom platform (students, parents, attendance, grade entry, messaging, announcements). Those features do not exist in this codebase at all — there is no students, parents, attendance, grades, enrollments, announcements, or messages table, and no UI for any of them. I will not invent reviews of screens that don't exist; instead I score what's built and report the rest as a feature-gap analysis.

0. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
What's actually built: email/password + (broken) OAuth auth, an onboarding wizard, subjects/chapters/lessons CRUD, a syllabus auto-parser, a DepEd-aware scheduling algorithm, a calendar (month + daily), AI activity generation (Gemini), a "library" of written-works/performance-tasks/exams, lesson-plan versioning/rebalancing, a tiered billing system (PayMongo/Stripe webhooks + quota-enforcing RPCs), and a read-only school-admin dashboard.

The engineering under the billing/quota layer and the scheduling algorithm is genuinely sophisticated. But the app is not launch-ready. There is a critical privilege-escalation hole, core auth flows (username login, password reset, OAuth) are broken, payments don't work in the launch market (PH), dark mode is unusable on key screens, and several headline features (vacancy fill, suspension display, version restore, admin CRUD, add-requirement) are dead, stubbed, or silently fail.

Production Readiness Score: 24 / 100.
Launch Recommendation: DO NOT LAUNCH — Internal Testing Only.

